      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable that you're looking for quick relief, especially with a consistent headache history, but it's really crucial to err on the side of caution during pregnancy. Even occasional use of ibuprofen can have risks for both you and your baby. Since you're feeling lightheaded and the cold compress isn't helping, it's best to delay taking further ibuprofen and instead take time to rest and try other non-medication strategies to find relief. Your health and your baby's health are paramount, and your doctor’s guidance is invaluable in these instances. It might be even more helpful to reach out to an urgent care center if you're having difficulty getting through to your doctor. Going to bed and resting might seem hard now, but it's for both of you of utmost importance. Keep trying to relax and call your doctor when they're available. Remember, you're not overthinking—it’s important to be safe and get professional advice. Stay safe. Your baby is precious, and your health is no less important.",
